C driver without stored tokens. The first backfill reuses the unchanged `umf-core==0.10.0` wheel and sdist from `umf-v0.5.4`. Registry uploads run only in GitHub Actions.\n\nThe driver verifies tag/source, SHA256SUMS, GitHub digests, release pins and registry-compatible metadata before upload; it rejects collisions and verifies PyPI-served bytes. SDK releases retain their separate SDK/core identities and single-wheel limit. Standalone `python-vX.Y.Z` releases require an explicit selected file/hash map, accept a qualified wheel cohort and reject raw Linux platform tags before upload. A separate consumer requires a published wheel from public PyPI. Release events and successful owned producer runs dispatch the driver, including token-created releases. No package version or tag changes.\n\nIntegrated main after runtime PR #49 at `3fd8c61c`. Canonical regeneration preserves all 578 source-module, 127 Rust-module and 76 Rust-build-input records from that qualified tree. The only inventory additions are four publisher scripts; a retired workflow activation edge is removed. Local inventory check, Rust boundaries (587 checked, zero findings, nine negative controls), reference boundaries (26 files), 13 publisher controls and both inherited filesystem stage tests pass. Scoped independent publisher review is clear. Original 0.10.0 archives passed the validator and Twine; scoped lint, formatting, Actionlint, YAML and diff checks passed. Final-head hosted publisher controls pass; hosted inventory/site integration checks remain queued. The broader local reference suite used stale generated output (70 versus 71 extensions), so it is not claimed as passing.\n\nApproved environment/publisher settings are configured; actual upload/consumer receipts remain pending. Native Core 0.10.2 qualification remains owned by its separate release lane; publication will preserve its accepted cohort and platform scope.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-